# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
__MACOSX/
*.swp
.obsidian/workspace*
.obsidian/cache

# --- Obsidian config ---
# The Wranglitdark theme is tracked (it is authored work, and it needs history
# so a bad edit can be diffed and reverted). Everything else under .obsidian
# is either machine-local state or third-party plugin code:
#   - plugins/*/data.json carries empty-but-present API-key slots, so it must
#     never be tracked: one paste into Copilot's settings would commit a key.
#   - plugins/*/main.js is vendored plugin code, not ours to version.
#   - graph.json is per-machine view state. appearance.json IS tracked:
#     it is what enables the Wranglitdark theme on first open.
.obsidian/plugins/
.obsidian/graph.json
# Editor-local scratch backups of the theme (bak-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM).
.obsidian/themes/**/*.bak-*

# --- Secrets (NEVER commit) ---
# Excludes .env at any depth (e.g. Expansions/<slug>/.env). Keys-only
# templates are kept tracked via the negation below.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
# ...but always ship the keys-only example template:
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
# Local MCP server configs may embed credentials — never commit:
.mcp.json
**/.mcp.json
.cursor/mcp.json
# Private keys / certs:
*.key
*.pem
id_rsa

# --- Derived database mirror & SQLite sidecars ---
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Dependencies & build artifacts ---
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
.cache/
*.tsbuildinfo
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Logs & runtime state ---
*.log
logs/
tmp/
*.pid

# --- Machine-local state (never part of the vault) ---
# Nightly Cockpit DB snapshots — regenerated locally, not shared history:
Backups/
# Remember-plugin session buffer / pointer:
.remember/

# --- Office lock / owner files (never commit) ---
~$*

# --- Team Inbox: raw client drops (live on disk, never in git) ---
# It is a drop zone: inputs get filed into PKM and removed. The filed
# knowledge is the asset, not the source workbook.
Team Inbox/*
!Team Inbox/README.md

# --- Client working data: never in git ---
# Raw client data (ledger exports, financial detail, anything with someone
# else's transactions in it) stays on disk. The analysis you produce from it
# is the durable record and IS tracked; the source extract is not.
#
# Every Deliverable folder may carry a _working/ subfolder for exactly this.
# It is visible in the file tree, but never committed.
Deliverables/*/_working/
# Project folders now hold filed deliverables (GL-009 7-ter), so ignore the
# client-data subfolders only, never the whole project.
copilot/projects/*/_working/
copilot/projects/*/*/_working/
copilot/projects/*/outputs/
